. Hence $\\overrightarrow{OX}=4\\mathbf{b}$.\n\nAlong $XC$, move $2$ squares left and $2$ squares up. A copy of $\\mathbf{a}$ moves $1$ square left and $1$ square up. Thus $XC=2|\\mathbf{a}|$ and the segment points in the same direction to $\\mathbf{a}$. Hence $\\overrightarrow{XC}=2\\mathbf{a}$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c}&=\\overrightarrow{OX}+\\overrightarrow{XC}\\\\&=4\\mathbf{b}+2\\mathbf{a}\\\\&=2\\mathbf{a}+4\\mathbf{b}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReorder the terms to match their vector names. Since $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, their coefficients are unique. Matching coefficients gives $\\lambda=2$ and $\\mu=4$." 13194139547580 17592186576411 true] [17592186761106 1080 "4" 13194139547580 17592186576411 true] [17592186761106 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139547580 17592186576411 true] [17592186761106 1083 #uuid "1c263ef5-1ded-5e06-b6a3-2ac7f032487b" 13194139547580 17592186576411 true] [17592186761107 1075 #edb/ref 17592186761119 13194139547580 17592186576411 true] [17592186761107 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139547580 17592186576411 true] [17592186761107 1077 "field-1" 13194139547580 17592186576411 true] [17592186761107 1078 #edb/ref 17592186761119 13194139547580 17592186576411 true] [17592186761107 1079 #uuid "20ba0dd4-3ff3-5622-b007-48317ee92b9f" 13194139547580 17592186576411 true] [17592186761108 1068 #edb/ref 17592186761118 13194139547580 17592186576411 true] [17592186761108 1068 #edb/ref 17592186761125 13194139547580 17592186576411 true] [17592186761108 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139547580 17592186576411 true] [17592186761108 1071 "The vectors are drawn on a square grid: $\\overrightarrow{OA}=\\mathbf{a}$, $\\overrightarrow{OB}=\\mathbf{b}$, and $\\overrightarrow{OC}=\\mathbf{c}$.\n\n![Vector diagram](images/a7/a7c8651a67d96846172792412818a0b3dca3b473ec064abbfc6a5ddc304be19e.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+\\mu\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$ and $\\mu$.\n\n$\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}\n\n$\\mu=$ {{fiel